# Force LF on disk for files whose parsers / runtimes break on CRLF.
#
# .scm:  GrammarCache::get_query splits the `; inherits:` directive on '\n'
#        only -- a stray '\r' in the parent name silently disables grammar
#        inheritance (cpp loses all C-derived highlights). The parser is
#        now CRLF-safe, but pinning the on-disk encoding is cheap defense.
# .sh:   shell scripts must be LF to execute on Unix CI runners.
*.scm  text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
